      "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/columncontrol/cols2_2-3_1-3",
      "col1": {
        "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
        "sling:resourceType": "wcm/foundation/components/parsys",
        "text": {
          "jcr:primaryType": "nt:unstructured",
          "jcr:createdBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
          "jcr:lastModifiedBy": "frank.mastrangelo@stryker.com",
          "jcr:created": "Thu Jun 15 2017 13:45:04 GMT-0400",
          "text": "<p>Used with the T2 Tibial Nailing System, the T2 Tibia Suprapatellar Instrument System offers an alternate method for the insertion of tibial (SPI) nails in a suprapatellar approach with the patients in a semi-extended position.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>T2 Tibia SPI offers two size options of drill sleeve available to accommodate nail diameters 8-13mm</li>\n<li>Elastic nail insertion sleeves designed to serve as working channel to protect joint space<br>\n</li>\n<li>WCH-coated fixation k-wires designed for secure fixation in tibial plateau to prevent anteriorization and back out of sleeves during reaming&nbsp;<br>\n</li>\n</ul>\n",
          "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Aug 23 2017 15:20:39 GMT-0400",
          "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
          "textIsRich": "true"
        }
      },
